From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wosnxn123 <wosnxn123@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 23:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lecithin: restore blocked plugin APIs at the Bukkit boundary

Ported from LophineLabs/Lecithin dev/26.2@fd9e884 paper-patches 0002-0012, 0014
(TinyYana, GPL-3.0 via inheritance chain). Lecithin 0013 (scoreboard) is NOT
ported: Canvas upstream already opens the scoreboard API with ensureMainThread
guards - an equivalent implementation.

fd9e884 (generalise the legacy sync scheduler shim to execution provenance)
replaces the per-plugin jar-SHA rule table (old 0003) with a single question -
"on whose behalf is this thread running" - answered by
LecithinExecutionProvenance: region thread -> that region, global tick thread
-> global region, startup thread -> global region, async PlayerEvent dispatch
-> that player's EntityScheduler (PaperEventManager now establishes the owner
for the whole dispatch and removes it in a finally), async platform events
with no player -> global region. Bare async threads and second hops still
fail closed. BukkitTask#cancel and scheduler cancelTask(s) now also cancel the
redispatched task via LecithinDispatchedTasks. Economy guard keys on the Vault
service interface instead of jar hashes.

Restores at the Bukkit/CraftBukkit boundary:
- Bukkit async scheduler semantics + diagnostic guard (0002) driven off the
  global tick (FoliaGlobalRegionScheduler heartbeat)
- execution-provenance sync scheduler dispatch (0003/0005/0014, fd9e884)
- per-account economy serialization (0003); Entity#teleport at the API
  boundary (0004); embedded PaperLib environment (0006); PaperPermissionManager
  locking (0007)
- riding-target dismount before teleport (0008) and mid-handover teleport
  wait (0009, D-40), adapted to Canvas's PluginTeleportAsyncState flow
- async task context inheritance (0010); console dispatch to global region (0011)
- cross-region block read from resident chunk (0013)

Canvas-side hardening (production incident 2026-08-18, TPA double-teleport
killed a region tick): a PluginTeleportAsyncState left behind by a REFUSED
teleport was never cleared, and the next teleport's guard then threw
IllegalStateException straight through EntityScheduler.executeTick. Now:
stale plugin states are replaced instead of throwing (foreign handoffs still
throw), failed futures clear their own state, and the scheduled teleport
lambda resolves the future instead of letting exceptions kill the region.

All behavior gated by canvas-server.yml plugin-compat.* (default true, see
GlobalConfiguration.PluginCompat). Canvas adaptations: contexts re-anchored
onto Canvas's region-threading code (transfer states, ensureMainThread
guards); config refs rewritten from Lecithin's Luminol TOML.

